=== sg_sanitize ===
USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  sg_sanitize [--ause] [--block] [--count=OC] [--crypto] [--dry-run]
      [--early] [--fail] [--help] [--invert] [--ipl=LEN] [--overwrite]
      [--pattern=PF] [--quick] [--test=TE] [--timeout=SECS] [--verbose]
      [--version] [--wait] [--zero] [--znr] DEVICE


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  DEVICE


FLAGS (21) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Where
-A, --ause       set AUSE bit in cdb
-B, --block      do BLOCK ERASE sanitize
-c, --count OC   OC is overwrite count field (from 1 (def) to 31)
-C, --crypto     do CRYPTOGRAPHIC ERASE sanitize
-d, --desc       polling request sense sets 'desc' field (def: clear 'desc'
                 field)
-D, --dry-run    to preparation but bypass SANITIZE commnd
-e, --early      exit once sanitize started (IMMED set in cdb) user can
                 monitor progress with REQUEST SENSE
-F, --fail       do EXIT FAILURE MODE sanitize
-h, --help       print out usage message
-I, --invert     set INVERT bit in OVERWRITE parameter list
-i, --ipl LEN    initialization pattern length (in bytes)
-O, --overwrite  do OVERWRITE sanitize
-p, --pattern PF PF is file containing initialization pattern for OVERWRITE
-Q, --quick      start sanitize without pause for user intervention (i.e. no
                 time to reconsider)
-T, --test TE    TE is placed in TEST field of OVERWRITE parameter list
                 (def: 0)
-t, --timeout SECS SANITIZE command timeout in seconds
-v, --verbose    increase verbosity
-V, --version    print version string then exit
-w, --wait       wait for command to finish (could take hours)
-z, --zero       use pattern of zeros for OVERWRITE
-Z, --znr        set ZNR (zone no reset) bit in cdb
